From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:46:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 45/92] Recycle host-copied textures' images that the host
 writes too

host_placed_image made each Shared or Managed texture's host-transfer image
directly (placed_image_read), bypassing the image recycler the non-host
images already use. Images the host writes too (host_reads=false) now go
through recycled_image with the hosted plan, whose HOST_TRANSFER usage
already separates their making from non-host images; a miss is
placed_image's, as before. Images the host only reads (a trapping surface's,
possibly in non-coherent memory with atom padding) keep the direct path and
are never parked or taken: their making does not tell those placements apart.

The recycler's bounds, last-holder parking, UNDEFINED hand-over and the
host zeroing of new textures are unchanged. Tests on the CPU ICD: a
recycled host-copied texture reads zero on the host and through a blit;
sixty frames make images in the first frame alone; an uncommitted command
buffer's texture is not parked until it completed and went.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
